# Never / Always

## Never
- Rewrite large subsystems without explicit need
- Duplicate components, utilities, hooks, or services
- Add dependencies without stated justification
- Touch unrelated files
- Guess when the repo can be inspected
- Claim tests/lint/typecheck passed if not run
- Commit or log secrets
- Silently change architecture, schema, or public contracts

## Always
- Inspect → search → reuse before creating
- Make the smallest correct change
- Preserve existing behavior unless the task changes it
- Handle errors consistently with local patterns
- Review your own diff
- State assumptions and residual risks
- Protect the demo path under time pressure
